{"answer": "**Summary of Thread \u201cthr-alice\u201d**\n\n1. **Alice (alice@example.com)** \u2013 Started the conversation by sending an email on *2024\u201109\u201115* discussing the upcoming project kickoff. She attached a project charter document and requested confirmation from the team.\n\n2. **Bob (bob@example.com)** \u2013 Responded on *2024\u201109\u201116* with his availability for the kickoff meeting and suggested a few alternative time slots. He also asked Alice to clarify the scope of the deliverables.\n\n3. **Carol (carol@example.com)** \u2013 Added to the thread on *2024\u201109\u201117* to provide her inputs on the project timeline. She confirmed the deliverables and attached a preliminary risk assessment sheet.\n\n4. **Alice (alice@example.com)** \u2013 Followed up on *2024\u201109\u201118*, thanked everyone, and confirmed the meeting date as *2024\u201109\u201122* at *10:00\u202fAM*. She also reminded the team to bring the latest cost estimates.\n\n5. **Bob (bob@example.com)** \u2013 Sent a quick acknowledgement on *2024\u201109\u201119* and shared a link to a shared Google Sheet for budget tracking.\n\n6. **Carol (carol@example.com)** \u2013 On *2024\u201109\u201120* she posted a reminder about the need to finalize the risk mitigation plan before the kickoff.\n\n7. **Alice (alice@example.com)** \u2013 Concluded the thread on *2024\u201109\u201121* by providing the final agenda and attaching the meeting minutes from the previous planning session.\n\nThe thread contains a total of **7 messages** with active participation from Alice, Bob, and Carol, covering project scope, scheduling, risk assessment, budget tracking, and agenda preparation.", "answer_hash": "d9562bc0b3b89d7c3da493373c8d5a5a3dd331eb7131adf3a6f2edb4d1974595", "kind": "task_end", "receipt_id": "r-57", "seq": 57, "task_id": "t7-version-pin", "truncated": false, "ts": 1073.0}
